 prompt='''Engineering implementation only, not skill Evolution. Return JSON {"files": {"filename": "complete file content"}, "notes": []}. Produce complete minimal changes to our supplied adapter for the nine task_specs. No placeholders. Do NOT edit SKILL.md, Evolution code, task questions, verifier, gold or scoring. We froze the new skill before any of these unseen tasks. No questions, gold or answers are supplied. Prefer the smallest working solution: for SOLVING use the existing Profy host as uid1000, subprocess cwd in the owned case directory, HOME in its owned case root and task-local Python PATH. Do NOT use PRoot and do not add any privileged solver launcher. Logical /root or /app paths from the original question map to owned case fs directories; make this common operational mapping clear and identical across all groups. The existing root kernel namespace is only for the fixed unchanged GRADER. Generalize its fixed task-directory mounts to /root and /app as necessary, without exposing credentials or changing grading logic. Preserve freeze/export-before-verifier and exact original-source hash checks.\nData: select only literal Dockerfile COPY input files plus Dockerfile from pinned rows BEFORE creating the archive. Never package the whole environment; xlsx-recover-data has groundtruth outside its COPY inputs. Support directory-copy semantics. For pdf-excel-diff use the exact two original public download URLs in the plan, no synthetic data, record hashes and require all groups to match A input hashes. Add explicit --target-skill xlsx so alphabetical first PDF skill never gets replaced by XLSX content. Validate requested target exists and --expected-parent-md-sha matches before paid work. Keep original other skills and resources unchanged.\nTransport: complete archive max50MB RAM, split into <=450000-byte chunks only if needed, upload serially, verify ordered piece hashes and total SHA256 before extraction; delete cloud staging after use. No local images/builds/cache.\nDependencies: native Profy system disk is about1GB, VM cgroup cap4GB. Do not attempt image-in-RAM. Install only task explicit apt packages with --no-install-recommends as a DISCLOSED native adaptation, temporary download cache on owned workspace then remove, apt simulation+free-space guard first. Full LibreOffice no-recommends is feasible: about451MB fresh footprint. Do not mutate the system Python or use --break-system-packages. Create a task venv with host system-site-packages and pin permitted declared pip requirements through existing uv, --no-cache, per-case cloud storage. Platform forbids reportlab,fpdf,fpdf2,python-pptx,pptxgenjs: do not install/use/bypass them. Record declared-but-omitted blocked packages in runtime disclosure and use permitted tools, identical restrictions across groups. Keep an actual dependency-version receipt. Use the same task interpreter/PATH for original grading where its script doesn't create its own pinned uvx env.\nExports: original task logical files at /root or /app, compare initial hashes, exclude dependencies/skills/control/cache/backup-only clutter as appropriate without changing requested outputs. Keep native metadata actual, no fake Docker image IDs. Absolute [OUTPUT] paths are REQUIRED by the platform collector. Preserve CLI compatibility for the existing single-task development mode. Add only necessary flags e.g. --native-specs and --expected-input-hashes. Keep all API execution/model calls serial. Do not change payment, purchase services, touch keys, or introduce hidden answer-derived logic. Add small offline tests for COPY selection, no groundtruth leakage, directory copy, target selection, chunk reassembly. Existing imports LibraryStudy chooses alphabetical skill; override safely in DockerStudy after construction and update target+args consistently. No tests mirroring trivial code. Include task_specs.json derived from the plan, without copying full third-party Dockerfiles/programs into our private repo. Do not start any paid run. JSON only.'''
 body={'model':'openai/gpt-6.1-sol','max_tokens':24000,'response_format':{'type':'json_object'},'messages':[{'role':'system','content':prompt},{'role':'user','content':json.dumps({'plan':json.loads(Path(a.plan).read_text()),'our_code':source},ensure_ascii=False)}]}
